  "note": "First election of the urban district council (the old town commissioners all sought re-election except Patrick Hughes, J.P., and John Nicholson); poll on Monday 16 January 1899. Surnames only, as printed. 293 names on the register, \"about 250\" voted. The Armagh Guardian, 20 January 1899, p. 2, also reports the Keady election (not read)."
